    <description>DIR-1782: V7 base (delegates Opportunity stage transitions to RES_OpportunityStageUpdateValidation) plus a RES_Config_Switch__c gate and bundle-aware validation: a Quote may have only one root unit/bundle. ParentQuoteLineItemId is NOT yet populated on bundle component lines at insert time (the platform links them in a later step), so root detection also excludes lines whose PriceWaterfallIdentifier starts with "ref_" - the constraint engine's marker for a component line it derived, as opposed to the "QLI{n}_0__0"-style identifier (or the "swap_in_line_item_0"-style identifier used during a unit swap) on the line the user actually selected. Root detection additionally excludes any line with Quantity &lt;= 0: a unit swap creates a -1 quantity line for the outgoing unit alongside a +1 line for the incoming one, and the outgoing line must not count toward the "one unit" limit. The line count is computed via Get_All_Quote_Line_Items_On_Quote (filtered on QuoteId only) + a Loop rather than a second SOQL filter on ParentQuoteLineItemId, because the platform rejects a QuoteLineItem query WHERE clause that includes ParentQuoteLineItemId once QuoteId stops being a single-value equality match - which is exactly what happens when Flow bulkifies this record-triggered flow across QuoteLineItem inserts spanning multiple Quotes in one transaction.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
